<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/18th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Revolution</p><h1 class="enc-title">Brabant Revolution</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1789">1789</a>–<a href="/years/1790">1790</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Brabant Revolution was an uprising in the Austrian <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-the-netherlands">Netherlands</a> against the centralising and church reforms of Emperor Joseph II. Beginning in Brabant in 1789, rebels drove out the Austrian forces and in January 1790 proclaimed the United Belgian States. Divisions between conservatives and democrats weakened the new state, and Austrian troops restored control in December 1790.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/brabant-revolution.jpg" alt="Brabant Revolution" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Anno16 · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_the_Brabantine_Revolution.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>After the <b>Brabant Revolution</b> of 1789–1790, French revolutionary armies occupied the region, and on 1 October 1795 the county was annexed by France and divided into the departments of Lys and Escaut.</blockquote><a href="/empire/county-of-flanders">County of Flanders · Decline &amp; Fall</a></li><li><blockquote>Its memory revived in the <b>Brabant Revolution</b> of 1789.</blockquote><a href="/empire/duchy-of-brabant">Duchy of Brabant · Global &amp; Regional Impact</a></li><li><blockquote>An émigré army from the Dutch Republic invaded the Austrian Netherlands, beginning the <b>Brabant Revolution</b> against Emperor Joseph II's centralising and church reforms.</blockquote><a href="/today-in-history/october-24">24 October in history</a></li><li><blockquote>Joseph II's centralising and church reforms sparked the <b>Brabant Revolution</b> of 1789 and the short-lived United Belgian States.</blockquote><a href="/state/austrian-netherlands">Austrian Netherlands</a></li></ul></section>
